   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Gunmen attacked a funeral inside a church in Jordan. Who were they?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Friday, at least seven people were killed in the village of Hammoud, near Karak, in southern Jordan. The Associated Press reports forty wounded. CNN and Fox News put the death toll at nine. The gunmen opened fire during a funeral at a Greek Orthodox church."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Jordan's government spokesman said the attackers followed an extremist takfiri ideology. Officials call them unknown assailants so far. No group has claimed responsibility. Security forces are hunting the gunmen. One witness said the shooting lasted about five minutes."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "King Abdullah vowed the harshest retaliation and ordered three days of national mourning. CNN calls the attack unprecedented, and says the toll was revised several times. Officials have not said whether the attackers had links to a terror group."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Jordan identify the attackers within a week? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
