  "title": "Gunmen Hit a Funeral in Jordan: Who Did It? #shorts",
  "description": "Gunmen opened fire at a Greek Orthodox church during a funeral in the village of Hammoud, Karak governorate, Jordan, on Friday, October 23, 2026. At least seven people were killed and about 40 wounded according to AP-based reports; CNN and Fox News report nine dead, so the toll is still being revised. Government spokesman Mohammad Momani said the attackers subscribed to an \"extremist takfiri ideology\". No group has claimed responsibility and no suspects have been named; a manhunt is under way. King Abdullah II vowed the \"harshest retaliation\" and Jordan declared three days of national mourning.\n\nSources:\nAP / NPR: Gunmen open fire at a church during a funeral in Jordan, killing 7 and wounding 40 (Oct 24, 2026)\nCBS News: At least 7 killed in attack on Jordan church during funeral (Oct 2026)\nCNN: At least 9 people killed in unprecedented shooting at church in Jordan (Oct 23, 2026)\nAl Jazeera: At least seven killed after gunmen open fire at church in Jordan (Oct 23, 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Jordan #MiddleEast #Karak",
